# cheeky-squad-os — .gitignore
#
# Patterns reflect what the plugin itself shouldn't track. If you're using
# this plugin on your own project, add the same .squad/ ephemeral patterns
# to that project's .gitignore.

# Ephemeral squad state — per-engagement working files, overwritten each
# dispatch. The deliverables they point at live in committed file_scope paths.
# (`.squad/features/*` was reserved in v0.1.0 and never defined; retired
# rather than carried forward undefined.)
.squad/role-comm-*
.squad/role-plan-*

# The partner model (hard rule #12) — a model of the human living in a git
# repo, and the source paper (§5.3) flags models of humans as dual-use.
# Gitignored by DEFAULT, not by enforcement: `squad-partner`'s create flow
# proposes this line and the file write as one write set, and the human can
# decline it. This is a default offer, not a mechanism — if you want your
# partner model committed, remove this line deliberately.
.squad/partner.md

# Generated worktrees from Multi-use mode (per Claude Code worktrees doc tip)
.claude/worktrees/

# Per-role sandboxes materialized by squad-env / provision.sh — ephemeral,
# recreated on each provision (the `environment` spec in roster.json is the
# committed source of truth; the materialized workspace is not).
.squad/workspaces/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor scratch
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# Logs and tmp
*.log
tmp/
.tmp/

# Node (if any tooling lands here later)
node_modules/

# Environment
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Python (if any tooling lands here later)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
